    "summary": "High‑energy San Diego ’82 with monster Other One & stellar Garcia solos",
    "review": "The February 19, 1982 gig at Golden Hall in San Diego is a fire‑cracker of the early‑’80s era. The band rides a high‑octane wave from the opening “Bertha” straight into a ripping first set – Jerry’s slide work on the break and a scorching “Little Red Rooster” solo have fans calling his tone “like a god.” Phil lays down an earthquake riff that fuels a monster second‑set jam, culminating in a space‑filled “Other One” that rockets through a seamless “Space > Other One” sequence before melting into a soulful “Stella Blue.” The pre‑drums improv and the Lost Sailor → Saint of Circumstance suite add extra mileage, while Brent’s keyboards sit perfectly in the mix, never swallowing Garcia’s lead. With tight drumming from Bill and Mickey, the whole night feels locked‑in, making this one of the standout shows of ’82.",
